# Two things share the name "cold start" and they are different sizes. The download is the part
# this project controls and it is drawn to scale against the part GitHub controls, which is drawn
# as an unknown on purpose rather than as a guess. The strip widths are the measured seconds.

title Where a reader's first minute goes

note code 40 70 920 60 "Measured on a 4 core runner at load 0.09, not on a Codespace." "The two boxes with a question mark are GitHub's and were not measured."

box own 40 170 200 90 "what the repo" "controls" "measured"
strip mine 260 170 230 90 "container start|0.19 s" "first build|4.5 s" "every build after|1.8 s"

box theirs 40 290 200 90 "what GitHub" "controls" "not measured"
strip gh 260 290 345 90 "provision a VM|?" "pull 0.70 GB|?"

arrow mine.0 gh.0 "the same clock"

note img 40 430 440 150 "The image is 1.7 GB unpacked" "and 0.70 GB compressed." "0.60 GB of the unpacked size" "is the base image's git and" "common-utils features, which" "no lesson here touches."

note lean 520 430 440 150 "The same image on a plain" "ubuntu base is 1.2 GB and" "0.50 GB compressed, in 10" "layers rather than 17, and" "it still produces a JitDump." "Not shipped yet, see the page."

note cost 40 610 920 90 "Cost to the project: 51 s of runner time to rebuild the image from nothing, 0 s when nothing changed." "Cost to a reader: 2 hours a day for thirty days fits in the free allowance on a 2 core machine." "The pilot lesson runs in 11.8 s once the container is up, and that is the number a lesson page inherits."

size 1000 720
